:"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10245","person_slug":"steve-georganas","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan Templeman","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10873","person_slug":"susan-templeman","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tania Lawrence","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10981","person_slug":"tania-lawrence","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ted O'Brien","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10866","person_slug":"ted-obrien","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Watts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10794","person_slug":"tim-watts","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Wilson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10894","person_slug":"tim-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tom French","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11039","person_slug":"tom-french","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tom Venning","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_11051","person_slug":"tom-venning","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Pasin","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10784","person_slug":"tony-pasin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tracey Roberts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10994","person_slug":"tracey-roberts","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Trish Cook","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11037","person_slug":"trish-cook","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zaneta Mascarenhas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10999","person_slug":"zaneta-mascarenhas","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zhi Soon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11049","person_slug":"zhi-soon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zoe McKenzie","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10976","person_slug":"zoe-mckenzie","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Migration Amendment (2026 Measures No. 1) Bill 2026 - Consideration in Detail - Agree to the bill","noes":8,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debate/?id=2026-03-11.27.6) *that the bill be agreed to.* This means they will now stop considering potential amendments and instead vote on whether to pass the bill. ### What does this bill do? According to the [bill homepage](https://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation/billhome/r7447), the bill: > *Amends the Migration Act 1958 to enable temporary restrictions on the arrival of certain classes of temporary visa holders in Australia, including when events or circumstances outside Australia mean that there is an increased risk that certain classes of temporary visa holders will not depart Australia when their visas cease to be in effect.* The [explanatory memorandum](https://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id:legislation/billhome/display.w3p;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fems%2Fr7447_ems_3693e0bf-117f-408a-bcc6-8abfdf540b86%22;rec=0) (which is a document prepared by the party introducing the bill, which is the Government in this case) explains that: > *Currently, the Migration Act does not contain a general power to prevent cohorts of non-citizens who hold visas that are in effect from traveling to Australia, including in circumstances where that travel may present a risk to Australia’s national interest,. Although there are powers under the Migration Act to cancel a non-citizen’s visa in those circumstances, those powers are only capable of being exercised in relation to individual non-citizens. The existing powers are therefore resource intensive, and are not suited to responding at scale to events occurring overseas where it is appropriate and in the national interest to limit or prevent travel to Australia for current holders of a temporary visa who are outside of Australia.* > > *This may include during periods of international conflict or other rapid international developments that place unsustainable strains on the fu","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-10046","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2026-03-11/4"}
